  "id": "20_Leaders_Who_Built_the_CISO_Era_2_Decades_of_Change_txt_110",
  "content": "Moss, 51, has always had a knack for providing a rich forum for the researcher community, starting with the very first DEF CON, which was basically a party in Vegas. Black Hat was created to bring together security researchers with the software companies they were hacking so they could better work together on solving security vulnerability problems. The conference has, of course, grown dramatically and expanded commercially over the years, but Moss's mission to bring together as many of the stakeholders in the industry as possible has continued at both shows, and in his work outside them.",
